(Why oh why don't my alpha testers find these problems?)

Murphy strikes again!  Right after I put out my last release, someone
reports a fairly major bug in lsattr.  You'll know if you have a bad
lsattr; just run it, and if you get back a bunch of "file not found"
error messages, you have the buggy version.  (Actually, the bug was in
libe2p shared library.)

I've put out another release of e2fsprogs 0.5c, dated 27-Oct.  If you're
grabbing e2fsprogs 0.5c from a mirror, look for the file
E2FSPROGS-0.5C-VERSION-IS-27-OCT.  That will tell you that it's pulled
over the latest verion of the file.

I apologize for the inconvenience.  With any luck, this should be the
final release of e2fsprogs 0.5c.

							- Ted


