Woven Goods for LINUX
                                  Announcement
 
- -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
This is the first BETA Release 0.1 of Woven Goods for LINUX. It is a collection
of World-Wide Web (WWW) Applications and Hypertext-based Information about
LINUX. It is ready configured for the Slackware Distribution and currently
tested with Version 2.3.0. The new LST 2.1 Distribution contains this
collection as an integral part with some changes.
 
The Collection consists of four Parts, so it can be used for multiple purposes
depending on the installed Parts:
 
  1. User-friendly browsing of locally available LINUX Documentation even if
     you are not connected to the Internet.
 
  2. Accessing world-wide available LINUX Documentation, WWW and FTP Servers,
     Linux Newsgroups and more. This is only possible if you are connected to
     the Internet.
 
  3. Providing LINUX Information via your own WWW Server. Again this is only
