                     REQUEST FOR DISCUSSION (RFD)
                   unmoderated group comp.sys.oric

This is a formal Request For Discussion (RFD) on the subject of creating an
unmoderated Usenet Newsgroup, comp.sys.oric

RATIONALE: comp.sys.oric

        The comp.sys.misc newsgroup is cluttered with PC and Macintosh
postings. Oric users currently hold discussions through e-mail and a mailing
list, but the different levels of interests (programming, using, meeting...)
show the need for a Usenet group. The mailing list has about 80 subscribers
today after two months of existence. It is little known because it is much
harder for people to find a mailing list than to 'grep' through a list of
active newsgroups. Oric sold about half a million computers and many users
are still developing new software. Also, the advent of Oric emulators for
Dos or Linux PC, Amigas and Unix/X11 workstations is the occasion for former
Oric users around the world to rediscover their favorite computer, and to
find that it is still the subject of very active development. (Many find it
hard to contemplate that other Oric enthusiasts live near to them.)
	However, the total postings expected for an Oric newsgroup should not
exceed 100 a day. This does not require several newsgroups; with a proper
thread discipline, comp.sys.oric is just the newsgroup we need.

CHARTER: comp.sys.oric

        To provide a forum for the discussion of every Oric-related subject:
the Oric1, Atmos and Telestrat computers, peripherals, one of the seven disk
operating systems available, emulators, programming techniques, games,
clubs, magazines, local events... The group will not be moderated.

END CHARTER.

PROCEDURE:

This message initiates a discussion period to consider the creation of
a comp.sys.oric newsgroup. Discussion will take place on news.groups.
If discussions are made in other newsgroups, they should always be
cross-posted to news.groups.

* This is not a call for votes. Please do not attempt to vote now.
  A call for votes (CFV) will we issued approximately 3 weeks after this RFD.
  When the CFV is posted, there will be instructions on how to mail your
  votes to the independant vote-taker.

DISTRIBUTION:

This RFD is in accordance with the Guidelines for Newsgroups Creation, and
has been cross-posted to the following relevant newsgroups:

news.announce.newsgroups, news.groups, comp.sys.misc,
comp.emulators.announce, comp.os.linux.announce, comp.os.msdos.misc



