LINUX SIG - ANNOUNCEMENTS
=========================
* Next meeting will be October 19th, 7:00pm at Open Computing
  Institute, Inc (See below for directions).

* The next meeting will feature a tutorial on the Linux File
  System Standard (FSSTND) followed by the first in a series of
  lectures - "Building a Linux System from Scratch".

* We will have the August release of Infomagic's Linux Developer's
  Resource (4-CD set) available for $25.00 a copy.  Also available
  for $15.00 will be `Linux - Guerrilla UNIX development' t-shirts.

* We are giving away copies of Caldera's Network Desktop v1.0 to
  artists of an original logo for the users group.  Check out the
  web page at http://dark.wustl.edu/sluugls for more details.



PRESENTATION DESCRIPTION
========================
As the first in the series, this lecture will discuss preparing
a system for Linux: creating a bootable partition with the required
utilities; migrating from an a.out compiler to ELF; and setting up
the necessary components of a base Linux system.  The Linux system
created will not rely on any prepackaged Linux distribution, will
be 100% ELF and will comply with the Linux File System Standard
everywhere possible.  Part of the discussion will focus on practices
to ensure system development and recoverability.




